{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015DTs5ncvm7CdFLcUg2fBzs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I couldn't find the exact AAAI scoring scale. Let me try fetching the AAAI-26 review process page or look for the standard AAAI scale. Based on my knowledge, AAAI typically uses a 1-10 scale:\n\n- 10: Strong Accept\n- 9: Accept  \n- 8: Accept\n- 7: Weak Accept\n- 6: Weak Accept / Borderline Accept\n- 5: Borderline / Weak Reject\n- 4: Weak Reject\n- 3: Reject\n\n\n- 2: Strong Reject\n- 1: Strong Reject\n\nThe context YAML mentions \"AAAI borderline accept (5.5-6.5/10)\" which confirms they use a 1-10 scale, so I'll go with the standard AAAI scoring system I'm familiar with.\n\nNow I need to set up the review process. I could dispatch two reviewers in parallel—one focusing on methods and experiments, another on novelty and related work—then run a roundtable discussion. But given that I have the full paper and context available, I think it's better to conduct a thorough review myself rather than risk having agents miss important nuances. Let me work through the complete roundtable process directly. I'm setting up the reviewer dispatch system to send both agents in parallel with the complete paper details, experimental results, and evaluation context they need to conduct thorough reviews.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":59888,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":444},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2badbab1-f12e-49d2-a949-e349aaeb2aba","uuid":"58c291a0-809f-4af5-9a56-536b6e3a14c9"}
